35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found eleven misrouted deliveries, all from duplicate addresses. Plus, we lose an hour daily copying records. It’s a real, daily loss.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, those daily losses are real, but my findings are worse. The coordination group is gutted, and past tools needing daily input were quietly abandoned.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your staffing concerns are valid, but my findings are worse. Half the customer sites lose network coverage for whole afternoons. We cannot build on sand.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, network issues are real, but my findings show the capital line is frozen. Only the recurring software allowance has room. We must fund this from that specific pocket.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@May, I found the pattern. Tools needing daily entry from everyone were quietly dropped. Narrow tools for one trade still run. We keep repeating this mistake.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, I hear you. But these daily losses are constant. If we don’t fix the data, the workload just keeps growing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, constant losses are exactly why we need a tool that doesn’t demand daily entry from everyone. My findings prove those get abandoned.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, abandoning tools is a choice. My data shows the physical infrastructure is broken. You cannot sync records if the signal vanishes for half the day.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, infrastructure is a constraint, not a budget. If the capital line is frozen, we cannot afford the expensive fixes you imply. We must work within the recurring allowance.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, infrastructure matters, but my data shows tools needing daily entry from everyone get abandoned. Narrow tools for one trade survive. We must avoid the broad trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, I agree. The narrow tools survive. My data shows the daily copying is the real drain. We need to stop the bleeding first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
